age":2.9,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.007797786616310587,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":21.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.4877179713957249,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013247066046423764,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.083129995,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":55.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Sonida Senior Living, Inc. owns and operates senior housing communities in the United States. The company provides independent living services, which include daily meals, transportation, social and recreational activities, laundry, housekeeping, and 24-hour staffing; and access to health screenings, periodic special services, and dietary and similar programs, as well as exercise and fitness classes. It offers assisted living services consist of personal care services, such as assistance with activities of daily living, including ambulation, bathing, dressing, eating, grooming, personal hygiene, and monitoring or assistance with medications; support services, such as meals, assistance with social and recreational activities, laundry, general housekeeping, maintenance, and transportation services; and supplemental services, which include extra transportation, personal maintenance, and extra laundry services, as well as special care services for residents with various forms of dementia. In addition, it offers memory care services; and home care services through third-party providers, such as customized physician, dentistry, podiatry, and other health-related rehabilitation and therapy services. Further, it provides respite care and temporary care and therapy programs. The company was formerly known as Capital Senior Living Corporation and changed its name to Sonida Senior Living, Inc. in November 2021. Sonida Senior Living, Inc. was founded in 1990 and is based in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brandon M. Ribar CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $980,822 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $111K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Sonida Senior Living, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.6B market cap on $381M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $9M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -11.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 29.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 8.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 165% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.650772200772201},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $10.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 72/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Sonida outlines plan to deploy about $250M of acquisition capital in 2026 while integrating CHP (NYSE:SNDA)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news